The gate can submit an empty patch on its first call: it accepts paths such as `tox.ini` and `testing/helper.py`, which the harness strips from the patch. A budget error also takes its unconditional-submit branch. The repeat metric issue is confirmed too: nested gate calls can break up identical root calls in the cited implementation.

